.Sh ENVIRONMENT
Options override the environment, which overrides the configuration file, which overrides
built-in defaults.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev CREATURE_WORLD_CONFIG
Configuration file, when
.Fl -config
is not given.
.It Ev SERVER_HOSTNAME , Ev SERVER_PORT
HTTP bind address and port.
.It Ev MONGODB_URI
MongoDB connection; the World keeps its events, facts, timers and scenes in the
.Li creature_world
database.
.It Ev OTEL_*
OpenTelemetry export (OTEL_SERVICE_NAME, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS,
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL). Without them the World logs to the console only.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/creature/world.json
Configuration: bind address, MongoDB, the Creature Server, scenes and when they open, house
asks and scenes, presence, regions, the calendar, reminders, memory, retention and facts.
A conffile; upgrades keep local edits.
.It Pa /etc/default/creature-world
Environment for the service, mode 0600. Secrets such as a MongoDB password or a telemetry
key live here and nowhere else.
.It Pa /usr/lib/systemd/system/creature-world.service
The unit. It runs as a
.Li DynamicUser
and is not started on install; review the configuration, then
.Dl systemctl enable --now creature-world
Override it with a drop-in in
.Pa /etc/systemd/system/creature-world.service.d/ .
.It Pa /usr/share/doc/creature-world/creature-world-manual.md
The operator's manual, including every configuration key.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run in the foreground against a local MongoDB:
.Dl creature-world --config /etc/creature/world.json --log-level info
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr creature-house 8 ,
.Xr creature-body 8 ,
.Xr creature-agent 8 ,
.Xr creature-communicator-gateway 8 ,
.Xr systemd.exec 5
